.TH "GIT-WORK" "1" "Apr 2019" "Generated from git-work's source code" ""

.SH NAME
git-work-user-me - Display the identity you write as


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit-work user me [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the identity this repository writes as, the one the first mutating
command settled from git's user.name and user.email.

.PP
This is the document work.user.me() returns; --format text prints the line
the bare \fBgit work user\fR prints for it.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-f\fP, \fB--format\fP="json"
	Select the output formatting style. Valid values are [json,text]

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for me


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgit-work-user(1)\fP
